.TH UBUNTU-DOCK-FOLDERS 1 "October 2026" "Ubuntu Dock Folders"
.SH NAME
ubuntu-dock-folders \- manage application folders for the desktop user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ubuntu-dock-folders enable
.RI [ --ubuntu-settings ]
.RI [ --system ]
.br
.B ubuntu-dock-folders uninstall
.br
.B ubuntu-dock-folders disable
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ubuntu Dock Folders groups application launchers on a desktop panel.
Run its commands from your desktop session as the logged-in user, without sudo.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B preferences
Open the grouping settings for the current desktop.
.TP
.B enable
Enable the installed desktop component.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the user's component and restore managed panel entries.
Folder settings and backups are retained. This does not remove the Debian package.
.TP
.B disable
Disable the desktop component and restore its managed launchers.
User files and folder settings are retained.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --ubuntu-settings
Add the grouping controls to Ubuntu Desktop settings in GNOME.
.TP
.B --system
In GNOME, use the Debian package's extension after backing up an installer-owned
user copy. Log out and back in to load the updated Shell code.
.SH SETTINGS
Open the Ubuntu Dock Folders application entry or the folder's gear button.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ubuntu-dock-folders-xfce (1)
.br
https://github.com/hawkab/ubuntu-dock-folders
